     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Two genders",
     "texto": [
      "- **en** = common gender, the most frequent.\n- **et** = neuter gender.\n\nThey don't match masculine and feminine. English nouns have no grammatical gender, so this is new for you: **en** kone (a wife), **en** søn (a son), **et** hus (a house). Learn each noun with its article."
     ],
     "tutora": "pensando"
    },
